ADS-010 — Metadata Model

Document ID: ADS-010
Title: Metadata Model
Version: 1.0.0-draft
Status: Draft

1. Purpose

This specification defines the Canonical Metadata Model (CMM) for the Atlas Engineering Cognition Framework (AECF).

The Canonical Metadata Model provides a standardized structure for describing, governing, discovering, securing, and tracing all Canonical Atlas Objects (CAOs).

Every CAO SHALL include metadata conforming to this specification.

2. Scope

This specification defines:

Metadata categories
Mandatory metadata
Optional metadata
Metadata inheritance
Metadata governance
Metadata quality
Metadata lifecycle

This specification applies to all Canonical Atlas Objects.

3. Canonical Definition

Metadata is structured information that describes, governs, identifies, classifies, manages, and traces a Canonical Atlas Object without altering its semantic content.

Metadata describes the object.

It is not the object itself.

4. Objectives

The Metadata Model SHALL:

Standardize object descriptions.
Enable discovery.
Enable governance.
Enable interoperability.
Support traceability.
Support lifecycle management.
Preserve provenance.
Enable automated processing.
5. Metadata Categories

Atlas defines seven canonical metadata categories.

Category	Purpose
Identity Metadata	Identifies the object
Descriptive Metadata	Describes the object
Governance Metadata	Defines ownership and policies
Lifecycle Metadata	Tracks operational state
Technical Metadata	Supports processing and interoperability
Provenance Metadata	Records origin and history
Discovery Metadata	Enables search and classification

All categories SHALL inherit from the Canonical Atlas Object.

6. Identity Metadata

Every CAO SHALL include:

Property	Description
Object ID	Globally unique identifier
Object Type	Canonical type
Namespace	Owning namespace
Version	Object version
Schema Version	Governing schema version

Identity metadata SHALL remain immutable except for version progression.

7. Descriptive Metadata

Every CAO SHALL define:

Title
Name
Description
Summary
Domain
Discipline
Keywords
Tags
Language
Documentation References

Descriptive metadata SHALL support both human and machine interpretation.

8. Governance Metadata

Every CAO SHALL include:

Owner
Steward
Custodian
Approval Authority
Security Classification
Access Policy
Retention Policy
Compliance Profile
Audit Policy

Governance metadata SHALL remain associated with the object throughout its lifecycle.

9. Lifecycle Metadata

Every CAO SHALL define:

Lifecycle State
Status
Created Timestamp
Modified Timestamp
Published Timestamp
Archived Timestamp
Retired Timestamp

Lifecycle transitions SHALL be recorded.

10. Technical Metadata

Technical metadata SHALL include:

Serialization Profile
Encoding
Checksum
Digital Signature Reference
Object Size
Compatible Schema Versions
Supported Profiles
Processing Requirements

Technical metadata SHALL remain independent of implementation technologies.

11. Provenance Metadata

Every CAO SHALL preserve:

Origin
Producer
Source Objects
Transformation History
Processing Engine
Responsible Workflow
Decision References

Provenance metadata SHALL be immutable.

12. Discovery Metadata

Discovery metadata SHALL support:

Classification
Taxonomy
Ontology References
Search Keywords
Domain Index
Geographic Scope (where applicable)
Temporal Scope
Related Objects

Discovery metadata SHALL facilitate efficient retrieval and knowledge exploration.

13. Metadata Inheritance

Every specialized Atlas object SHALL inherit the Canonical Metadata Model.

Canonical Atlas Object
        │
        ▼
Canonical Metadata Model
        │
 ┌──────┼──────────────┐
 ▼      ▼              ▼
CEA     DR            CEV
 │       │             │
 ▼       ▼             ▼
Inherited Metadata for All Objects

Specializations MAY add metadata but SHALL NOT remove mandatory metadata.

14. Metadata Lifecycle

Metadata SHALL progress through the following lifecycle.

Defined
   │
Validated
   │
Applied
   │
Maintained
   │
Versioned
   │
Archived

Metadata history SHALL remain auditable.

15. Metadata Quality Requirements

Metadata SHALL satisfy:

Completeness
Correctness
Consistency
Accuracy
Timeliness
Traceability
Interoperability
Discoverability

Quality SHALL be measurable.

16. Metadata Governance

Metadata SHALL be governed through:

Validation rules
Ownership
Stewardship
Change control
Audit
Retention
Compliance verification

Metadata governance SHALL be independent of payload content.

17. Conformance

A Canonical Atlas Object conforms to the Metadata Model if it:

Implements all mandatory metadata.
Preserves metadata integrity.
Supports inheritance.
Maintains provenance metadata.
Supports lifecycle metadata.
Implements governance metadata.
18. Future Evolution

Future revisions MAY introduce:

Semantic ontology bindings.
Knowledge graph metadata.
AI-generated metadata enrichment.
Automated classification.
Domain-specific metadata profiles.
Cross-enterprise metadata federation.

Extensions SHALL preserve canonical metadata semantics.

